  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.header": "Slugma Burners",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_1": "Slugma Burners are in all ways similar to Blaze Burners in terms of functionality.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_2": "To get a Slugma Burner, you must first capture a wild slugma and then click on it with an empty burner.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_3": "Alternatively, use the Throw Selected Pokémon hotkey while pointing at a placed empty burner while selecting a valid Slugma from your party.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_4": "To retrieve a Slugma from a burner, simply point at the burner and use the previous hotkey again.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_5": "Alpha Slugmas unfortunately don't fit inside one, same for its evolution, Magcargo.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_6": "Fueling a Slugma functions similarly to a blaze burner.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_7": "However, lower level Slugmas will have shorter burn time duration.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_8": "Higher level Slugmas will have their burn time significantly increased, with a Level 100 Slugma, a Lava Bucket makes it burn for more than half an hour.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_9": "Blaze cakes can also have their duration prolonged.",
  "create_encapsulated.ponder.slugma_burner.text_10": "Slugma Burners can also be fed automatically with Deployers or Mechanical Arms.",

